    {
      "text": "Noah was a just man and perfect, Gen. 6:9 (Moses 8:27). Just balances, just weights … shall ye have, Lev. 19:36. shall judge the people with just judgment, Deut. 16:18. a God of truth … just and right is he, Deut. 32:4. He that ruleth over men must be just, 2 Sam. 23:3. thou art just in all, Neh. 9:33. Shall mortal man be more just than God, Job 4:17. path of the just is as the shining light, Prov. 4:18. teach a just man, and he will increase, Prov. 9:9. through knowledge shall the just be delivered, Prov. 11:9. just shall come out of trouble, Prov. 12:13. wealth of the sinner is laid up for the just, Prov. 13:22. just weight and balance are the Lord’s, Prov. 16:11. just man walketh in his integrity, Prov. 20:7. that there be just men, Eccl. 8:14. way of the just is uprightness, Isa. 26:7. a just God and a Saviour, Isa. 45:21. that have shed the blood of the just, Lam. 4:13. if a man be just, and do that which is lawful, Ezek. 18:5. just shall live by his faith, Hab. 2:4 (Rom. 1:17; Gal. 3:11; Heb. 10:38). thy King cometh unto thee: he is just, Zech. 9:9.",
